<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:17:15Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany news: EU ministers meet for migration showdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1aae9e5f07fd83e167b69f62e98a0b25a6dadbf26a3995c899b076aa23ed26f</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T19:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-eu-ministers-meet-for-migration-showdown/live-79441034--691a60120f40.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-eu-ministers-meet-for-migration-showdown/live-79441034?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European interior ministers hold migration talks in Munich as the bloc plans to strengthen borders and speed up deportations. Meanwhile, trade unions staged nationwide demos against health and welfare cuts. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Backlash over data centers tests Europe's AI ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e685f3c48548164b20286e359f17eea48065503633af28be8805f0e0d8e2bdbd</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:16:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T18:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800--224361aa983d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/backlash-over-data-centers-tests-europe-s-ai-ambitions/a-79419800?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Massive data centers needed to run AI are triggering protests across Europe. Their operators counter that they boost digital sovereignty and energy independence.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China, US agree to set up channel for AI safety incidents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8201862ea874e2f4b1d9f256df231f8db32e3d38e683a2bb4a5f84feccfd89b4</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:16:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-us-agree-to-set-up-channel-for-ai-safety-incidents/a-79443351--116e0ce66bfc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-us-agree-to-set-up-channel-for-ai-safety-incidents/a-79443351?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following the summit between US President Donald Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping, the two superpowers pledged to set up a "communication channel" for AI incidents and boost coordination on military matters.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump rejects Iran proposal to reopen Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:377fe6ea9ec4e60cb4e5e4aaccf03e96f1c3de8fc8692fdb1e82e16b6846fc68</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:17:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-rejects-iran-proposal-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz/a-79444893--025adfe63f1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-rejects-iran-proposal-to-reopen-strait-of-hormuz/a-79444893?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump says he has rejected an Iranian proposal to reopen the Strait of Hormuz and put an end to hostilities. "I'd like to make a deal, too," he said. "But that deal would not be acceptable."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Paris: Pope Leo XIV celebrates Mass before huge crowd</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:79ba897ee50e7b3f0c6f44cd81d359aaafb5afd29e4761e6ff6853b07fe0cfe8</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:17:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T16:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/paris-pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-mass-before-huge-crowd/a-79442864--ce9a98bc1a48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/paris-pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-mass-before-huge-crowd/a-79442864?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pope addressed around 700,000 people during a Mass at the Place de la Concorde, near the Champs-Elysees. Leo XIV is on a four-day visit to France.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia expected to intensify hybrid war on Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f7196defa369cc3666acaa5f08a06eac4555408a0d1ed6564232c0a98f8d977</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:17:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T15:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-expected-to-intensify-hybrid-war-on-europe/a-79444596--b27c55cf76ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-expected-to-intensify-hybrid-war-on-europe/a-79444596?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Drone explosions, airspace violations, arson attacks: Poland, Romania, and Moldova are now regularly targeted in Russian attacks against Ukraine. More governments are calling these attacks deliberate acts of aggression.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's FM Wadephul meets Lavrov on UNGA sidelines</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:690c4ee7aeac6543fda1e279a792f8fd5acaaaa9f6155b1d78fa581e511c2ab1</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:17:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-fm-wadephul-meets-lavrov-on-unga-sidelines/live-79366211--0b50744a8e02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-fm-wadephul-meets-lavrov-on-unga-sidelines/live-79366211?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's the first such meeting since Russia launched the invasion of Ukraine in February 2022. DW has the latest on day 5 of the UN General Assembly debate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Suicide attack at police stop kills at least 11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0b31220f14af0763ade356f27ee398dbde9d875076dd6db05f9e3a724d21096</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:17:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-attack-at-police-stop-kills-at-least-11/a-79443050--24fa32f41a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-attack-at-police-stop-kills-at-least-11/a-79443050?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The blast was claimed by the Pakistani Taliban, which has stepped up attacks on Pakistani security forces in recent years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German Olympic Committee names Munich as bid city choice</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:30ef081fc029cba62edeae6cc035912db37be0b8ab083a60a09db78cb8cb823f</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T12:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-olympic-committee-names-munich-as-bid-city-choice/a-79441284--424a4614f81d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-olympic-committee-names-munich-as-bid-city-choice/a-79441284?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Munich has been voted as the city that will bid for the Olympics in 2036, 2040 or 2044. Berlin had been in the running but withdrew on Thursday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Propaganda in Russian schools prepares students to die</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b8a38dbc187d2429c502f32b0fe8c4a6719d9eeb05f3516b488a33b49eb2a7c</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/propaganda-in-russian-schools-prepares-students-to-die/a-79417294--eaf06d603c17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/propaganda-in-russian-schools-prepares-students-to-die/a-79417294?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Russian government wants children to learn about patriotism from an early age. DW spoke to students in Siberia about their views on propaganda, the war in Ukraine and their future.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea's gender pay gap grows as women get older</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea74da4e9bc5dece819f5b858fb00d607a051154d2b5d8a2750fcf89de133ed2</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T10:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285--9ddac1458d8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report shows how in South Korea, women on average earn less and have fewer employment opportunities throughout their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Deadly blast rips through Athens building, near Acropolis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d047352334275139af4384770010cc5681f7d8387ad01eb30e2618fd8d50e4c1</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T09:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/deadly-blast-rips-through-athens-building-near-acropolis/a-79441931--87a5e1705efa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/deadly-blast-rips-through-athens-building-near-acropolis/a-79441931?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several foreign tourists remain missing after an explosion brought down a building in Athens' tourist area of Plaka, with the city's mayor calling it an "incredible disaster."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: New Delhi, Islamabad trade accusations at UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dce8adffb6d5c90fd3c49ec7103088f693bf3eacad591ca13d4a21e0f774a445</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T07:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-islamabad-trade-accusations-at-un-general-assembly/live-79440869--5c329050c900.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-new-delhi-islamabad-trade-accusations-at-un-general-assembly/live-79440869?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Shehbaz Sharif criticized India's policy on Kashmir and praised Pakistan's military, while New Delhi accused Islamabad of supporting cross-border terrorism. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Thailand: Bangkok flooding triggers disaster declaration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f75ce834e226d464b28874f71b60c66649b9f8bae30e069dac0a6a39c6c16504</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T06:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/thailand-bangkok-flooding-triggers-disaster-declaration/a-79440575--24f35b64d6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/thailand-bangkok-flooding-triggers-disaster-declaration/a-79440575?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rainfall over the past three days has caused heavy flooding in the Thai capital. A state of disaster has been declared in all 50 districts in Bangkok.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>OpenAI tools post user images from ChatGPT online</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9953a04e5d7fab84cc1e83a5aef33edddf384ce6d4b3f72ef7ba5518bab45ef</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T05:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/openai-tools-post-user-images-from-chatgpt-online/a-79440406--854a7e11bf2e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/openai-tools-post-user-images-from-chatgpt-online/a-79440406?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">OpenAI said it found 53 cases in which user-uploaded image links on ChatGPT were shared with third-party websites. The company said it had removed most of these links.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>White House bars CNN from covering upcoming Trump trip, broadcaster says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2634cff6624842ffccef52685c081849f81e56e7f027b5fe6e3b09aaa4ca49c</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T03:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/white-house-bars-cnn-from-covering-upcoming-trump-trip-broadcaster-says/a-79440241--597a83f39a01.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/white-house-bars-cnn-from-covering-upcoming-trump-trip-broadcaster-says/a-79440241?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">CNN said its journalists have been barred from accompanying President Donald Trump on his upcoming trip to Tennessee. The episode marks the Trump administration's latest salvo against the major cable news network.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>TikTok agrees to settle with Alabama state over teen safety</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:92d889b5bcd3cd68c082195a8379618471bfdfb59efb7f3068819fbd0fdefe47</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T03:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tiktok-agrees-to-settle-with-alabama-state-over-teen-safety/a-79440240--8af3dd0cef0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tiktok-agrees-to-settle-with-alabama-state-over-teen-safety/a-79440240?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The settlement involves TikTok adding several child safety measures to its platform including time limits and increased parental control. It is similar to a recent settlement competitor Meta had reached.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Yemeni leader calls for general mobilization against Houthis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba09b8d7c6f153a503d12ee20662a824e37922db976a031e6104bd2e0c51a920</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T21:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemeni-leader-calls-for-general-mobilization-against-houthis/a-79439604--0bc1a71d540c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemeni-leader-calls-for-general-mobilization-against-houthis/a-79439604?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amid military escalation with the Iran-backed Houthis, the Saudi-backed head of Yemen's governing body urged his compatriots to join the government forces.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Lula or Bolsonaro as president? Brazil gears up to vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:003b74ab36b26cc1f80ae498cfea48daa7669fb3760427009fee815040ff600d</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T20:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lula-or-bolsonaro-as-president-brazil-gears-up-to-vote/a-79437276--a6f357f68a3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lula-or-bolsonaro-as-president-brazil-gears-up-to-vote/a-79437276?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brazilians go to the polls on October 4. The front-runners are multilateralist incumbent Lula da Silva and former President Jair Bolsonaro's son, Flavio, who wants to bring Brazil closer to the US and away from China.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Parliament approves fuel tax cut</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:495b0262215403271f61e3e0c9060556b98f641b13c8c2c8edacba43d10bea61</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T19:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-approves-fuel-tax-cut/live-79424882--bd35c461e842.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-parliament-approves-fuel-tax-cut/live-79424882?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German lawmakers hope to drive down fuel prices by cutting taxes on gas and diesel from October 1. Meanwhile, Germany's defense minister visited Budapest to ramp up defense and military ties.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iranian President Pezeshkian brought a diplomatic tone to New York for UNGA. What did his remarks signal?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8027eebd490d931726cdefc8b52e311e3471f2f217f270e7bfcecd97f71da0e3</id><updated>2026-09-26T19:15:59Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T18:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iranian-president-pezeshkian-brought-a-diplomatic-tone-to-new-york-for-unga-what-did-his-remarks-sig/a-79428890--b543693f4fe7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iranian-president-pezeshkian-brought-a-diplomatic-tone-to-new-york-for-unga-what-did-his-remarks-signal/a-79428890?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran's president used his trip to New York this week for the UN General Assembly to signal openness to talks over the nuclear dispute. However, the chances of a major breakthrough on the war remain low.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
